# Playwright per-run output. The HTML report and traces are debugging
# artifacts for one run against a throwaway fixture — never source.
#
# GLOB, NOT AN EXACT NAME. A trailing-slash pattern is a literal directory name:
# `playwright-report/` matched the smoke suite's output and never covered the
# canary's `playwright-report-canary/`. Combined with `git add -A`, that gap put
# four real Playwright traces into this branch's history carrying 36 plaintext
# password occurrences, 60 JWTs and 24 refresh-cookie entries. GitGuardian passed
# the PR — it does not scan inside a zip.
#
# The HTML report is credential-bearing BY CONSTRUCTION, not just when a trace
# rides along: Playwright embeds a base64 copy of the run inside `index.html` and
# renders step titles containing literal fill values, so a sign-in step reads
# `Fill "<the password>"`. There is no variant of these directories that is safe
# to commit, which is why the patterns are deliberately wide.
test-results*/
playwright-report*/
blob-report*/
.last-run.json

# Screenshots/videos the canary (#386) writes outside the report dir.
artifacts/
